  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Giens peninsula, in Hyères, is ringed by a coastal path that runs along wild coves, with sea views at every turn. It is managed by the Métropole Toulon Provence Méditerranée (TPM) and crosses a Conservatoire du littoral site, a protected Mediterranean forest. The TPM topoguide describes two walks on the peninsula: the loop around La Madrague harbour and the walk between La Badine and Darboussières beach (24 km round trip, 8 h, sporty level), with some difficult sections and a path that is sometimes steep. The leaflet "Balades sur la presqu'île de Giens" (2023 edition) adds two short circuits of 2.5 km and 3.7 km.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>For your dog, the rule is clear: the coastal path topoguide published by the TPM Métropole (online version of 24 July 2026), which the town of Hyères relays on its website, states "Dogs are banned on the coastal path and in the Port-Cros National Park". This ban covers the whole coastal path of the Métropole, including the tour of the Giens peninsula. The massif is closed to walkers on red or extreme fire-risk days; from 21 June to 20 September, the Métropole asks visitors to check access restrictions every day on the Var massifs map. The peninsula is a Conservatoire du littoral site managed by the Métropole with the technical and scientific assistance of the Port-Cros National Park; the Métropole asks visitors to stay on marked paths, wear suitable shoes and bring a cap and water.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: out of respect for the TPM rules, this path is not a place to walk your dog; head instead to the <a href="/en/fiche-hyeres-merou">Mérou dog beach</a> in Hyères.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Hyères and its beaches are nearby, notably the <a href="/en/fiche-hyeres-merou">Mérou dog beach</a>. On site, a <a href="/en/fiche-toiletteur-pat-toutou">groomer</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-camping-mediterranee-hyeres">Camping Méditerranée</a> round out a stay in the area nicely.</p>
    </div>

